WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.592
On this slide, we are focusing on data types tell python what values mean.

00:00:04.592 --> 00:00:09.247
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.247 --> 00:00:15.227
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.227 --> 00:00:20.452
A data type tells Python what a value means and which operations are valid.

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:28.892
Numeric values support arithmetic, strings represent text, and Boolean values represent True or False logic.

00:00:28.892 --> 00:00:32.112
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:37.187
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:42.202
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:42.202 --> 00:00:44.616
from the names and output.
